WEBVTT

00:00.120 --> 00:01.270
- [Instructor] We're told that Adam flew

00:01.270 --> 00:04.630
his remote controlled
drone off of a platform.

00:04.630 --> 00:08.560
The function f models
the height of the drone

00:08.560 --> 00:10.940
above the ground, in meters,

00:10.940 --> 00:15.860
as a function of time, in
seconds, after takeoff.

00:15.860 --> 00:17.610
So what they want us
to do is plot the point

00:17.610 --> 00:20.410
on the graph of f that corresponds to each

00:20.410 --> 00:21.580
of the following things.

00:21.580 --> 00:23.030
So pause the video and
see if you can do that,

00:23.030 --> 00:25.440
and, obviously, you can't
draw on your screen.

00:25.440 --> 00:27.320
This is from an exercise on Khan Academy,

00:27.320 --> 00:28.720
but you can visually look at it,

00:28.720 --> 00:30.930
and even with your
finger, point to the part

00:30.930 --> 00:35.420
of the graph of f that
represents each of these things.

00:35.420 --> 00:36.830
All right, so the first thing here

00:36.830 --> 00:39.650
is the height of the platform.

00:39.650 --> 00:43.630
So the drone is at the
height of the platform

00:43.630 --> 00:44.890
right when it takes off,

00:44.890 --> 00:47.610
'cause it says Adam flew
his remote controlled drone

00:47.610 --> 00:49.410
off of a platform.

00:49.410 --> 00:52.640
So what is the time that he's taking off,

00:52.640 --> 00:54.180
the drone, or the drone is taking off?

00:54.180 --> 00:56.320
Well, that's going to
be at time t equals zero

00:56.320 --> 00:57.153
right over here.

00:57.153 --> 00:59.490
And what is the height of
the drone at that moment?

00:59.490 --> 01:01.150
It is 60 meters.

01:01.150 --> 01:03.690
So that must be the
height of the platform.

01:03.690 --> 01:05.670
So that point right over there tells us

01:05.670 --> 01:06.890
the height of the platform.

01:06.890 --> 01:09.310
And if they asked us what the
height of the platform is,

01:09.310 --> 01:11.240
it would be 60 meters.

01:11.240 --> 01:14.650
The next one is the
drone's maximum height.

01:14.650 --> 01:16.120
So then as time goes on,

01:16.120 --> 01:17.650
we can see the drone starts going

01:17.650 --> 01:19.420
to a higher and higher and higher height,

01:19.420 --> 01:21.070
gets as high as 80 meters.

01:21.070 --> 01:23.520
And then it starts going down.

01:23.520 --> 01:27.110
So it looks like 80
meters, at time 10 seconds,

01:27.110 --> 01:31.140
the drone hits a maximum
height of 80 meters.

01:31.140 --> 01:33.040
And then last but not least,

01:33.040 --> 01:36.870
they say the time when the
drone landed on the ground.

01:36.870 --> 01:38.480
Now, we can assume that the ground

01:38.480 --> 01:41.520
is when the height of the
drone is at zero meters,

01:41.520 --> 01:44.430
and we can see that that
happens right over here.

01:44.430 --> 01:47.950
And that happens at time
t equals 30 seconds.

01:47.950 --> 01:49.570
And so we've just marked it off,

01:49.570 --> 01:50.880
and I know what some of
you all are thinking.

01:50.880 --> 01:52.330
Wait, there's another time

01:52.330 --> 01:55.420
where the drone's height is at zero,

01:55.420 --> 01:56.470
and that's right over here.

01:56.470 --> 01:58.410
That's at negative 10 seconds.

01:58.410 --> 01:59.950
Couldn't we say that that's also a time

01:59.950 --> 02:01.530
when the drone landed on the ground?

02:01.530 --> 02:04.220
And this is a important point to realize,

02:04.220 --> 02:05.260
because if we're really trying

02:05.260 --> 02:06.910
to model the drone's behavior

02:06.910 --> 02:09.140
from time t equals zero,

02:09.140 --> 02:11.230
if t equals zero is
right when you take off

02:11.230 --> 02:12.870
all the way to it lands,

02:12.870 --> 02:15.770
then this parabola that we're
showing right over here,

02:15.770 --> 02:17.680
it actually, we would probably want

02:17.680 --> 02:20.660
to restrict its domain to positive times.

02:20.660 --> 02:22.950
And so this negative time
region right over here

02:22.950 --> 02:24.910
really doesn't make a lot of sense.

02:24.910 --> 02:28.940
We should probably consider
the non-negative values

02:28.940 --> 02:30.870
of time when we're trying to think

02:30.870 --> 02:32.783
about these different thins.
